Implement the scramble integration pipeline that builds and injects the scramble functionality when requested:

1. Import the necessary scramble functions (dynamically to avoid dependency errors):
```typescript
async function integrateScramble(config, optimizationResult) {
  // Dynamically import scramble functions to avoid dependency errors
  // when scramble is not installed
  const { buildScramble, injectScrambleIntoHtml } = require('@tw-enigma/scramble');

  logger.info('Building scramble with configuration...');

  // Build scramble with user configuration
  const scrambleResult = await buildScramble({
    speed: config.scrambleSpeed || 100,
    debug: config.scrambleDebug || false,
    // Pass other scramble configuration options
  });

  logger.info('Injecting scramble into HTML files...');

  // Inject scramble script into HTML files
  const injectionResult = await injectScrambleIntoHtml({
    buildDir: config.buildDir,
    scrambleScript: scrambleResult.script,
    dryRun: config.dryRun,
  });

  logger.info(`Scramble integration complete!`);
  logger.info(`- HTML files injected: ${injectionResult.filesInjected}`);

  return {
    ...optimizationResult,
    scrambleEnabled: true,
    scrambleFilesInjected: injectionResult.filesInjected,
  };
}
```

2. Integrate this function into the main command action:
```typescript
.action(async (options) => {
  try {
    // Previous steps: load config, validate, optimize CSS, detect scramble

    let result = optimizationResult;

    // Integrate with scramble if requested and available
    if (validatedConfig.scramble && isScrambleAvailable) {
      result = await integrateScramble(validatedConfig, result);
    }

    // Log final results
    logger.info('Enigma optimization complete!');
    if (result.scrambleEnabled) {
      logger.info('Scramble integration: Enabled');
    }

    // Command completion

  } catch (error) {
    logger.error(`Error during scramble integration: ${error.message}`);
    process.exit(1);
  }
});
```

This implementation should follow the scramble PRD integration sequence exactly, ensuring that scramble is only integrated when explicitly requested with the `--scramble` flag.

